				773,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Replace hardcoded output event strings with typed SkyEvent constants\n\nReplace hardcoded \"sky://output/*\" string literals in ChannelContent.rs and\nChannelLifecycle.rs with typed constants from CommonLibrary::IPC::SkyEvent.\n\nThis includes:\n- sky://output/append -> SkyEvent::OutputAppend\n- sky://output/replace -> SkyEvent::OutputReplace\n- sky://output/clear -> SkyEvent::OutputClear\n- sky://output/create -> SkyEvent::OutputCreate\n- sky://output/dispose -> SkyEvent::OutputDispose\n\nUsing the SkyEvent enum ensures consistency across the codebase and reduces the risk of typos in event names.",
			"SHA": "176f750a8d8a3cfc649d5958645021379085c5f4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T00:39:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				773,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Split monolithic IPC handlers into modular domain structure\n\nBreak up the 167KB WindServiceHandlers.rs into domain-specific modules:\n- Commands, Configuration, Extensions, FileSystem, Model, NativeHost\n- Navigation, Output, Search, Storage, Terminal, UI, Utilities\n\nSimilarly refactor CocoonService/mod.rs from a 2800-line monolithic impl to delegate to domain modules:\n- Auth, Command, Debug, Extension, FileSystem, Initialization\n- Output, Provider, Save, SCM, Secret, Task, Terminal\n- TreeView, Window, Workspace\n\nEach domain module now owns its specific RPCs, improving maintainability and enabling parallel development on different handler domains. The dispatch remains a thin one-line delegate per typed RPC.",
			"SHA": "346842c23cbf13208a7afc941aad7ae08f4f301a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T00:18:58Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				773,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Remove accidental .bak backup file\n\nDelete Source/Track/Effect/CreateEffectForRequest.rs.bak which was\ninadvertently staged in the Source/Track/Effect directory. The file\nwas zero bytes and appears to be a leftover from development work.\n\nThis cleans up the Mountain source tree.",
			"SHA": "f92b8538e62527ef86a7d474b794795054528edd"
		}
	],
